  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Companies pay for people who bridge the lab and the market. They judge you by accuracy, plain explanation and respect for rules.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is explaining one scientific idea in two sentences to a person outside the field.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and careers that combine science and business: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools summarise papers, draft documents and answer product questions. Routine documentation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Scientific judgment, trust and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to summarise and draft; later, own claims and customer relationships.
  </p>

